 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** $O(1)$ per triangle. The algorithm performs a fixed number of vector operations (subtractions, cross products, dot products) and one division [S3, S10, unofficial].
+- **Time Complexity:** $O(1)$ per triangle. The algorithm performs a fixed number of vector operations (subtractions, cross products, dot products) and one division [S3, unofficial][S10, unofficial].
 - **Memory Complexity:** $O(1)$ auxiliary space. It does not require precomputed plane equations or additional data structures beyond the triangle vertices [S10, unofficial].
 - **Performance:** It is considered one of the fastest ray-triangle intersection routines for triangles without precomputed plane equations [S10, unofficial]. Optimized variants exist that delay division or handle sign checks differently, but the core logic remains the same [S3, unofficial].
-- **Strengths:** Minimal storage, no need to compute plane equations, robust handling of barycentric coordinates directly [S3, S10, unofficial].
-- **Limitations:** Does not inherently handle back-face culling (requires caller intervention) [S9, unofficial]. Numerical stability depends on the choice of epsilon and the scale of the scene [S1, S3, unofficial].
